From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:16:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] images: use ANGLE on lavapipe when the vendor has no
 SwiftShader

With no DRM render node and no host gralloc, make_base_props() writes
ro.hardware.egl=swiftshader. The current MAINLINE vendor image
(lineage-20.0-20261022) ships no SwiftShader: its egl directory holds
ANGLE and Mesa, and hw/ has Mesa's lavapipe as vulkan.lvp. libEGL then
finds no renderer, and SurfaceFlinger aborts with "couldn't find an
OpenGL ES implementation".

The base props are written before the vendor image is mounted.
make_prop() runs once it is, so check there what the image carries. If
SwiftShader is absent and ANGLE and lavapipe are both present, ask for
ANGLE on lavapipe instead.

On the BraX3, which has a KMS-only card0 and no render node, Android
now boots, rendering through ANGLE on llvmpipe.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/helpers/images.py | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/helpers/images.py b/tools/helpers/images.py
index 21712cb..2c78879 100644
--- a/tools/helpers/images.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/images.py
@@ -185,6 +185,23 @@ def make_prop(args, cfg, full_props_path):
     if not props:
         raise RuntimeError("waydroid_base.prop is broken!!?")
 
+    # Without a render node make_base_props() asks for SwiftShader, which the
+    # current MAINLINE vendor images no longer ship - they have ANGLE and
+    # Mesa's lavapipe instead, and libEGL then finds no renderer at all. The
+    # base props are written before the vendor image is mounted; here it is,
+    # so check what it really carries and use ANGLE on lavapipe if that is
+    # what is there.
+    vendor = tools.config.defaults["rootfs"] + "/vendor"
+    def vendor_has(path):
+        return any(os.path.isfile(vendor + lib + path) for lib in ["/lib64/", "/lib/"])
+    if "ro.hardware.egl=swiftshader" in props and \
+            not vendor_has("egl/libEGL_swiftshader.so") and \
+            vendor_has("egl/libEGL_angle.so") and vendor_has("hw/vulkan.lvp.so"):
+        props = [p for p in props
+                 if not p.startswith(("ro.hardware.egl=", "ro.hardware.vulkan="))]
+        props.append("ro.hardware.egl=angle")
+        props.append("ro.hardware.vulkan=lvp")
+
     def add_prop(key, cfg_key):
         value = cfg[cfg_key]
         if value != "None":
